From 79cf1d2d312e84f5e0b9c46f3b89c192a5716cdd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ParkWardRR <alfa147x@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 13:06:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 15/50] qualcommax: ipq807x: add engenius,ews377ap-v3 to
 02_network (single 2.5G lan)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

WiFi confirmed fully working on hardware (both radios AP+STA, 23dBm) — the
'hang' was a false negative (radios register as phy2/phy3; only iw dev was
empty). The remaining gap was board.d: our board hit the *) default
('Unsupported hardware'), so network/board.json weren't set up and wifi
auto-config was blocked. Add it to the single-lan AP group (like wax218/
eap660hd). WiFi generates correctly via wifi config once radios are up.
---
 .../linux/qualcommax/ipq807x/base-files/etc/board.d/02_network   | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/target/linux/qualcommax/ipq807x/base-files/etc/board.d/02_network b/target/linux/qualcommax/ipq807x/base-files/etc/board.d/02_network
index de072424fe..ec9899a081 100644
--- a/target/linux/qualcommax/ipq807x/base-files/etc/board.d/02_network
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommax/ipq807x/base-files/etc/board.d/02_network
@@ -60,6 +60,7 @@ ipq807x_setup_interfaces()
 	netgear,sxs80)
 		ucidef_set_interfaces_lan_wan "lan2 lan3 lan4 lan5" "wan"
 		;;
+	engenius,ews377ap-v3|\
 	netgear,wax218|\
 	netgear,wax620)
 		ucidef_set_interface_lan "lan" "dhcp"
